					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-726895#post-4831468</guid>
				<title>SCP-1459: </title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-726895/scp-1459#post-4831468</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 29 Nov 2020 17:10:53 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kothardarastrix</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3460794</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This is a scout for some kind of extra dimensional invasion, sent here to learn every possible way humans kill things so the invading soldiers can prepare. Every time they test this machine, they are making it harder to repel this eventual invasion. However, as long as we keep testing it regularly, the invasion won’t happen, not until they’re sure they’ve seen every possible means of being killed. This is why SCP-001-EX said testing should continue indefinitely.</p> <p>Optionally, the invading species are the puppies. The machine can’t repeat termination methods because they adapt immediately.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
